  "body": "## What changed\n- A Face operation with \"Do not touch\" items is now refused when the keep-out blocks a facing level.\n- The refusal names the protected items, Cut Z and the depth that the face can reach.\n- The refusal tells the user what to do: set Cut Z to the reached depth, use a smaller clearance, or remove the item.\n- The old note \"blocked N facing level(s); the remaining levels stayed clear\" is removed. It can no longer occur.\n- `face_keep::Tally` records the lowest level that is cut and the lowest level that is asked for.\n- The decision is in `docs/decisions/3526-face-keep-depth.md`.\n\n## Cause\n- The keep-out of a level covers the heights from that level up to the clearance plane.\n- Thus a lower level gets the same keep-out or a larger one, and the blocked levels are always the lowest levels.\n- When a lower level was blocked, the Face generated anyway. The face stopped above Cut Z everywhere.\n- Only a note said so. Nothing marked the operation, and the post was not blocked.\n\n## Why a refusal\n- A `Toolpath` has no \"incomplete\" state. It has notes only, and the app and the post read no note as a state.\n- An \"incomplete\" state is a change to the cache, the project file, the status line and the post gate. That is too large for this defect.\n- The issue permits a refusal. A refusal is visible and blocks the post.\n- The workaround is direct: Cut Z at the reached depth faces clean.\n\n## Tests\n- Pin: `face_keep::a_keepout_that_blocks_the_lower_levels_refuses_with_the_depth_reached` (crates/motion/tests/face_keep.rs).\n  - The keep-out changes with Z: a 12 mm box above Z -1.5, and the whole face below it. Levels are Z -1 and Z -2 (Cut Z).\n  - The test asserts the refusal, the item name, \"Cut Z -2.000\" and \"Z -1.000\".\n- Pin proof (mutation): with `face_keep.rs` from upstream/main, the pin FAILS. The face generated at Z -1 only, with the note \"blocked 1 facing level(s)\". With the fix, the pin PASSES.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on head 07b9d2f9b: green, 25 steps, 0 failed. This includes motion `face_keep`, `face_holes`, `face_blend`, `top_z_level`, and app `do_not_touch_face`, `example_catalog`, `solid_law_goldens`, `first_part_programs`.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main` on head 07b9d2f9b: the plan has 101 steps (motion heavy and app heavy). The run stopped at the 2-hour tool limit during step 80.\n  - Steps 1-79: 78 ok, 1 failed.\n  - The failure: `pocket3d_hsm::the_users_bore_roughs_adaptive_level_by_level_and_verifies_clean`, \"the mesh behind the Linux path pin\", left 5232, right 6228.\n  - This count is the imported mesh. It is read before any toolpath is made, so a Face change cannot move it. Open issue #3085 tracks this count band.\n  - Steps 80-101 (app heavy, after `rotary_field_parity`) did not run.\n\n## Goldens moved\n- None. The quick gate ran `example_catalog`, `solid_law_goldens` and `first_part_programs` on the final head, and all passed with no change.\n\n## Not exercised\n- An app-level test with a real model that is wider below the face. The motion pin uses a Z-dependent keep-out closure. This is the same input that the app gives to `face_over_kept`.\n- Heavy steps 80-101 (see above).\n\n## Overlaps\n- None. No open PR changes `face.rs`, `face_keep.rs` or `crates/motion/tests/face_keep.rs`.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: A Face with \"Do not touch\" items is now refused, with the depth that it can reach, when an item blocks the lower facing levels. Before, the face stopped above Cut Z and only a note said so.\n\nFixes #3526\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
